      <string id="PrimaryPassword">Primary (Master) Password</string>
      <string id="PrimaryPassword_Explain">Require or prevent using a Primary Password.

Require or prevent using a primary (formerly master) password.

If this value is true, a primary password is required. If this value is false, it works the same as if DisableMasterPasswordCreation (#disablemasterpasswordcreation) was true and removes the primary password functionality.

If both DisableMasterPasswordCreation and PrimaryPassword are used, DisableMasterPasswordCreation takes precedence.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#primarypassword
</string>
      <string id="PromptForDownloadLocation">Prompt for download location</string>
      <string id="PromptForDownloadLocation_Explain">Ask where to save files when downloading.

Ask where to save each file before downloading.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#promptfordownloadlocation
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Mode">Proxy method</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Mode_Explain">The proxy method being used.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Mode_none">No proxy</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Mode_system">Use system settings</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Mode_manual">Manual configuration</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Mode_autoDetect">Auto-detect (WPAD)</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Mode_autoConfig">Automatic proxy configuration (PAC)</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Locked">Lock the proxy settings</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Locked_Explain">Prevents the user from changing the proxy settings.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_AutoConfigURL">Automatic proxy configuration URL</string>
      <string id="Proxy_AutoConfigURL_Explain">Only used if the proxy method is autoConfig.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_FTPProxy">FTP proxy (deprecated)</string>
      <string id="Proxy_FTPProxy_Explain">Deprecated.

This setting has no effect, because support for FTP proxies was removed.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_HTTPProxy">HTTP proxy</string>
      <string id="Proxy_HTTPProxy_Explain">The HTTP proxy server.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_SSLProxy">SSL proxy</string>
      <string id="Proxy_SSLProxy_Explain">The SSL proxy server.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_SOCKSProxy">SOCKS proxy</string>
      <string id="Proxy_SOCKSProxy_Explain">The SOCKS proxy server.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_SOCKSVersion">SOCKS version</string>
      <string id="Proxy_SOCKSVersion_Explain">The SOCKS version.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_SOCKSVersion_4">SOCKS v4</string>
      <string id="Proxy_SOCKSVersion_5">SOCKS v5</string>
      <string id="Proxy_UseHTTPProxyForAllProtocols">Use the HTTP proxy for all protocols</string>
      <string id="Proxy_UseHTTPProxyForAllProtocols_Explain">Whether the HTTP proxy is also used for all other protocols.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Passthrough">No proxy for</string>
      <string id="Proxy_Passthrough_Explain">Hostnames or IP addresses which are not proxied, separated by commas. Use &lt;local&gt; to bypass proxying for all hostnames which do not contain periods.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_UseProxyForDNS">Proxy DNS when using SOCKS v5</string>
      <string id="Proxy_UseProxyForDNS_Explain">Use the proxy for DNS requests when using SOCKS v5.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="Proxy_AutoLogin">Don't prompt for authentication if the password is saved</string>
      <string id="Proxy_AutoLogin_Explain">If the proxy requires authentication and its password is saved, Thunderbird logs in without asking. If that login fails, the user is asked again.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#proxy
</string>
      <string id="RequestedLocales">Requested locale</string>
      <string id="RequestedLocales_Explain">Set the list of requested locales for the application in order of preference.

The corresponding language packs become active.

Note: This policy can also be a string, so that you can specify an empty value.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#requestedlocales
</string>
      <string id="RequestedLocalesString">Requested locale (string)</string>
      <string id="RequestedLocalesString_Explain">Set the list of requested locales for the application in order of preference.

The corresponding language packs become active.

Note: This policy can also be a string, so that you can specify an empty value.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#requestedlocales
</string>
      <string id="SearchEngines_Add_1">New search engines (1)</string>
      <string id="SearchEngines_Add_1_Explain">Adds search engines to the built-in ones.

Although there are only five engines available in the ADMX template, there is no limit. To add more in the ADMX template, you can duplicate the XML.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#searchengines

Name: The name of the search engine (required).

Icon URL: The icon to use.

Alias: A keyword to use for the engine.

Description: A description of the search engine.

Encoding: The query charset for the engine. It defaults to UTF-8.

Method: The HTTP method.

Search URL: The search URL with {searchTerms} to substitute for the search term (required).

POST data: The POST data as name value pairs separated by &amp;.

Suggestions URL: A search suggestions URL with {searchTerms} to substitute for the search term.
</string>
