      <string id="SearchEngines_Remove">Hidden search engines</string>
      <string id="SearchEngines_Remove_Explain">These built-in search engines are not offered to the user.

The search engines are given by their names. They are hidden when the policy is applied for the first time and whenever the list changes.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#searchengines
</string>
      <string id="SearchEngines_Default">Default search engine</string>
      <string id="SearchEngines_Default_Explain">The search engine which is used to search the web from Thunderbird.

The search engine is given by its name, either a built-in search engine or one added with Add. It is set when the policy is applied for the first time and whenever the name changes, so the user can choose another default search engine in the meantime.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#searchengines
</string>
      <string id="SearchEngines_DefaultPrivate">Default search engine for private browsing</string>
      <string id="SearchEngines_DefaultPrivate_Explain">The search engine which is used in private browsing.

This setting has no effect in Thunderbird.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#searchengines
</string>
      <string id="SearchEngines_PreventInstalls">Prevent search engine installs</string>
      <string id="SearchEngines_PreventInstalls_Explain">Webpages can't install search engines.

This setting has no effect in Thunderbird.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#searchengines
</string>
      <string id="SecurityDevices_Add">PKCS #11 modules to add</string>
      <string id="SecurityDevices_Add_Explain">The names of the devices to add, with the paths of their libraries.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#securitydevices
</string>
      <string id="SecurityDevices">Add PKCS #11 modules (older form) (deprecated)</string>
      <string id="SecurityDevices_Explain">Deprecated.

The older form of this policy, with the names of the devices to add directly in the policy.

It is still supported, but ignored if Add or Delete is used.

Environment variables like %USERPROFILE% are expanded.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#securitydevices
</string>
      <string id="SecurityDevices_Delete">PKCS #11 modules to delete</string>
      <string id="SecurityDevices_Delete_Explain">The names of the devices to delete.

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#securitydevices
</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMax">Maximum SSL version enabled</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMax_Explain">Set the maximum SSL version.

Set and lock the maximum version of TLS. (Thunderbird defaults to a maximum of TLS 1.3.)

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#sslversionmax
</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMax_tls1">TLS 1.0</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMax_tls1_1">TLS 1.1</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMax_tls1_2">TLS 1.2</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMax_tls1_3">TLS 1.3</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin">Minimum SSL version enabled</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin_Explain">Set the minimum SSL version.

Set and lock the minimum version of TLS. (Thunderbird defaults to a minimum of TLS 1.2.)

For more information visit: https://thunderbird.github.io/policy-templates/policies/esr153/#sslversionmin
</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin_tls1">TLS 1.0</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin_tls1_1">TLS 1.1</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin_tls1_2">TLS 1.2</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin_tls1_3">TLS 1.3</string>
